<title>UK: BTI sets call and put currency warrants.</title>
<headline>BTI sets call and put currency warrants.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>BT Effecten GmbH has issued American-style call and put warrants of 500,000 per tranche on dollar cross rate, lead manager Bankers Trust International Plc said.</p>
<p>The warrants are on sterling/dollar, dollar/yen, dollar/mark and dollar/Swiss franc. Maturity date for the warrants is May 28, 1998 and payment date is June 11, 1997. They are all listed on the Frankfurt stock exchange and are available in minimum exercise lots of 100.</p>
<p>-- Reuter London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
